body:
- Tool agent event context contains a serializable AIAgentError instance. This type hides important details about an exception, e.g., the exact type of the exception. Replaced this serializable type with a Throwable instead and transform to AIAgentError when needed;
- Renamed `throwable` to `error` on Agent/Node/Subgraph failed contexts and pipeline parameters for consistency across lifecycle events;
- Switched `onToolValidationFailed` and `onToolCallFailed` pipeline signatures to accept Throwable;
- Added a custom serializer for ToolResultKind.Failure / ValidationError that encodes a Throwable through AIAgentError, preserving the existing JSON wire format;
- Updated OpenTelemetry span and metric helpers to take Throwable directly, fixing a latent `error.type` attribute that always reported AIAgentError as the exception class;

closes: [KG-815](https://youtrack.jetbrains.com/issue/KG-815)

## Summary

- Introduce `RetroLLMFit`, a Retrofit-inspired factory that generates a fully-wired `LLMClient` at runtime from annotated request/response data classes
- Eliminates ~50–100 lines of boilerplate required for every new LLM provider integration — only URL, field names, and auth differ
- Supports flat completion, chat, tool calling (OpenAI + Anthropic formats), and SSE streaming — all driven by annotations
- **Open by design**: message serialisation is a pluggable `MessagesSerializer` interface, not a closed enum — any wire format (Gemini, custom internal API, etc.) is supported without changing the framework

## New module

`prompt/prompt-executor/prompt-executor-clients/prompt-executor-retrollmfit`

### Request annotations

| Annotation | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `@LLMEndpoint(url, authHeaderName?, authHeaderValue?, authQueryParam?, authQueryValue?)` | Marks the request class; supports both header and query-param auth; URL may contain `{model}` placeholder |
| `@PromptField` | Injects the flat prompt string (all messages joined) |
| `@MessagesField(serializer)` | Injects messages via a custom `MessagesSerializer` implementation — default is `OpenAIChatSerializer` |
| `@ModelField` | Injects `LLModel.id` |
| `@ToolsField(format)` | Injects tool definitions (OpenAI or Anthropic wire format) |
| `@StreamField` | Toggles SSE streaming |

### Response annotations

| Annotation | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `@ResponseTextField` | Flat field extraction |
| `@ResponseText("choices[0].message.content")` | Dot-path extraction with array indexing |
| `@ResponseFinishReason("choices[0].finish_reason", toolCallValue = "tool_calls")` | Detects tool-call vs text; `toolCallValue` is configurable (Anthropic uses `"tool_use"`, Gemini `"TOOL_USE"`) |
| `@ResponseToolCalls("choices[0].message.tool_calls")` | Extracts tool-call array |
| `@ResponseStreamDelta("choices[0].delta.content")` | Per-chunk SSE delta path |

### Flat API example (Jaika)

```kotlin
@LLMEndpoint(
    url = "https://my-llm-server/api/prompt",
    authHeaderName = "X-User-Id",
    authHeaderValue = "your-user-id",
)
@Serializable
data class JaikaRequest(
    @PromptField val prompt: String,
    val stream: Boolean = false,
)

@Serializable
data class JaikaResponse(
    @ResponseTextField val text: String,
    val session_id: String = "",
    val type: String = "",
)

val client = RetroLLMFit.create<JaikaRequest, JaikaResponse>()
val response = client.execute(prompt, RetroLLMFitModel)
// response = [Message.Assistant("Jaika here, your dedicated AI assistant.")]
```

### OpenAI-compatible example (chat + tools + streaming)

```kotlin
@LLMEndpoint(url = "https://api.openai.com/v1/chat/completions",
             authHeaderName = "Authorization", authHeaderValue = "Bearer $KEY")
@Serializable
data class ChatRequest(
    @ModelField    val model: String = "gpt-4o",
    @MessagesField val messages: List<JsonObject> = emptyList(),
    @ToolsField    val tools: List<JsonObject>? = null,
    @StreamField   val stream: Boolean = false,
)

@ResponseText("choices[0].message.content")
@ResponseFinishReason("choices[0].finish_reason")
@ResponseToolCalls("choices[0].message.tool_calls")
@ResponseStreamDelta("choices[0].delta.content")
@Serializable
data class ChatResponse(val choices: List<JsonObject> = emptyList())

val client = RetroLLMFit.create<ChatRequest, ChatResponse>()
// client.execute(), client.executeStreaming(), client.execute(…, tools) all work
```

### Anthropic example (configurable finish-reason value)

```kotlin
@ResponseFinishReason("stop_reason", toolCallValue = "tool_use")  // Anthropic uses "tool_use"
@ResponseToolCalls("content", format = ToolFormat.ANTHROPIC)
```

### Custom message format (BYO serializer)

```kotlin
// Zero framework changes needed for any new API
object GeminiSerializer : MessagesSerializer {
    override fun serialize(messages: List<Message>): List<JsonObject> =
        messages.filter { it !is Message.System }.map { msg ->
            buildJsonObject {
                put("role", if (msg is Message.Assistant) "model" else "user")
                put("parts", buildJsonArray { add(buildJsonObject { put("text", msg.content) }) })
            }
        }
}

@MessagesField(GeminiSerializer::class)
val contents: List<JsonObject> = emptyList()
```

### Query-param auth example (e.g. `?key=…`)

```kotlin
@LLMEndpoint(
    url = "https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/models/{model}:generateContent",
    authQueryParam = "key",
    authQueryValue = System.getenv("GEMINI_API_KEY"),
)
```

## Resilience note

Because the request and response classes are the source of truth, a breaking change in any provider's API (OpenAI, Anthropic, Gemini, or a custom internal server like Jaika) only requires updating the data class annotations — the framework itself does not need to change.

## Test plan

- [x] 14 unit tests (MockEngine, no network) — all passing
- [x] Live integration test against Jaika server — passing
- [x] Explicit API mode (`explicitApi()`) satisfied
- [x] Sources in `jvmCommonMain` — compiles for both JVM and Android

