> Activates dormant `EnvironmentToAgentTerminationMessage` and `AIAgentTerminationByClientException` infrastructure to deliver production-ready agent cancellation with semantic outcomes.

```mermaid
graph TB
    A[User API] --> B[Core Agent Execution]
    B --> C{Execution Outcome}

    C --> D[✅ Success]
    C --> E[❌ Failure] 
    C --> F[🛑 Cancelled]

    G[Dormant Infrastructure] --> F

    style A fill:#e1f5fe
    style B fill:#f3e5f5
    style C fill:#fff3e0
    style G fill:#e8f5e8
```

## Problem & Solution

**Before:** Koog had unused termination infrastructure (`EnvironmentToAgentTerminationMessage`) and exception classes (`AIAgentTerminationByClientException`) that were never integrated into agent execution.

**After:** Complete agent interruption system with tri-state outcomes, automatic termination message creation, and pipeline-based event handling integrated with Koog's core architecture.

## Usage Examples

### **Comprehensive Usage Example**
```kotlin
// 🎯 Complete agent cancellation workflow
suspend fun processUserRequest(agent: AIAgent<String, String>, userInput: String) {
    // 1. Timeout protection for long-running tasks
    val outcome = agent.runWithTimeout(userInput, timeout = 30.seconds)

    when (outcome) {
        is RunOutcome.Success -> {
            logger.info("Agent completed: ${outcome.value}")
            respondToUser(outcome.value)
        }

        is RunOutcome.Cancelled -> {
            // Semantic handling based on cancellation reason
            when (outcome.reason) {
                CancellationReason.UserRequested -> 
                    logger.info("User cancelled operation")
                CancellationReason.Timeout -> 
                    logger.warn("Operation timed out after 30s")
                CancellationReason.Policy -> 
                    logger.error("Policy violation detected")
                CancellationReason.System -> 
                    logger.error("System-level cancellation")
            }
            respondWithCancellation(outcome.reason, outcome.cancelledAt)
        }

        is RunOutcome.Failure -> {
            logger.error("Agent failed", outcome.error)
            respondWithError(outcome.error)
        }
    }
}

// 2. External cancellation for interactive scenarios
suspend fun startInterruptibleAgent() {
    val cancellableExecution = agent.startCancellable("Long running task")

    // User can cancel via CLI, web interface, etc.
    keyboardListener.onEscapePressed { 
        cancellableExecution.cancel(CancellationReason.UserRequested)
    }

    val outcome = cancellableExecution.outcome.await()
    handleOutcome(outcome)
}

// 3. Kotlin Result compatibility for existing codebases  
suspend fun kotlinResultIntegration() {
    val result: Result<String> = agent.runCatching("input")

    result
        .onSuccess { value -> processSuccess(value) }
        .onFailure { error -> 
            if (error is AgentCancelledException) {
                handleCancellation(error.reason) // Preserves semantic context
            } else {
                handleError(error)
            }
        }
}
```

### **Automatic Termination Messages**

Agent cancellation now automatically creates termination messages and integrates with Koog's pipeline:

```kotlin
// ✅ Basic usage - termination messages created automatically
val agent = AIAgent(executor, llmModel, systemPrompt = "You are a helpful assistant")

val outcome = agent.runWithTimeout("Process this request", 30.seconds)
when (outcome) {
    is RunOutcome.Cancelled -> {
        // EnvironmentToAgentTerminationMessage already created automatically
        println("Agent cancelled: ${outcome.reason}")
    }
    // ... handle success/failure
}
```

### **Pipeline Integration for Custom Logic**

Advanced users can extend termination handling through Koog's core event system:

```kotlin
// Custom feature that handles termination events
object CustomTerminationFeature : AIAgentFeature<EmptyConfig, CustomTerminationHandler> {
    override fun install(config: EmptyConfig, configure: EmptyConfig.() -> Unit) = 
        CustomTerminationHandler()
}

class CustomTerminationHandler {
    fun createAgentHandler() = AgentHandler(this).apply {
        agentTerminationHandler = AgentTerminationHandler { context ->
            // Custom termination logic
            when (context.reason) {
                CancellationReason.Timeout -> notifyAdmins("Agent timeout: ${context.agentId}")
                CancellationReason.UserRequested -> logUserCancellation(context.runId)
                else -> handleOtherTerminations(context)
            }

            // Send to external monitoring system
            externalMonitoring.reportTermination(context.agentId, context.reason)
        }
    }
}

// Install the feature
val agent = AIAgent(...) {
    install(CustomTerminationFeature) { }
}
```

## Technical Implementation

**Core Architecture**: Tri-state outcome system (`Success`/`Failure`/`Cancelled`) with semantic `CancellationReason` enum, structured concurrency compliance, and cooperative cancellation checkpoints throughout the execution pipeline.

**Message Integration**: `AIAgent.sendTermination()` automatically creates `EnvironmentToAgentTerminationMessage` instances and integrates with Koog's core pipeline event system through `AgentTerminationContext` and `AgentTerminationHandler`.

**Compatibility**: 100% backward compatible - all existing `agent.run()` calls continue working unchanged. New cancellation APIs are purely additive.

