> Comprehensive checkpoint evolution for Koog agents that enables safe strategy upgrades with versioned migrations, automatic hash validation, and backwards compatibility.

This PR introduces a production-ready checkpoint migration system for Koog agents that handles strategy evolution through versioned migrations, cryptographic hash validation, and flexible message history policies. The system enables safe agent deployments with evolving graph structures while maintaining full backwards compatibility.

## Architecture Overview

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    A[Load Checkpoint] --> B{Version Check}
    B -->|Same Version| C{Hash Check}
    B -->|Older Version| D[Apply Migrators]
    B -->|Newer Version| E[❌ Reject with Error]

    D --> F{Migration Successful?}
    F -->|Yes| G[Update Version Metadata]
    F -->|No| H[❌ Migration Failed]

    G --> C
    C -->|Hash Match| I[✅ Set Execution Point]
    C -->|Hash Mismatch| J[⚠️ Log Warning]
    J --> I

    I --> K[Resume Agent Execution]

    style A fill:#e1f5fe
    style E fill:#ffebee
    style H fill:#ffebee
    style I fill:#e8f5e8
    style J fill:#fff3e0
    style K fill:#e8f5e8
```

## Comprehensive Example

Complete migration system integration showing all capabilities working together:

```kotlin
// 1. Define checkpoint data structure with versioning
@Serializable
data class AgentCheckpointData(
    val checkpointId: String,
    val createdAt: Instant,
    val nodeId: String,
    val lastInput: JsonElement,
    val messageHistory: List<Message>,
    // NEW: Version metadata (backwards compatible)
    val strategyId: String? = null,
    val graphVersion: Int = 1,
    val graphHash: String? = null,
    val customMeta: Map<String, String> = emptyMap()
)

// 2. Create migrators for strategy evolution
class NodeRenameMigrator : CheckpointMigrator {
    override suspend fun migrate(data: AgentCheckpointData, toVersion: Int): AgentCheckpointData {
        val newNodeId = when (data.nodeId) {
            "old_onboarding" -> "user_onboarding"
            "legacy_validation" -> "input_validation"
            else -> data.nodeId
        }
        return data.copy(
            nodeId = newNodeId, 
            graphVersion = toVersion,
            customMeta = data.customMeta + ("migrated_at" to Clock.System.now().toString())
        )
    }
}

class InputFormatMigrator : CheckpointMigrator {
    override suspend fun migrate(data: AgentCheckpointData, toVersion: Int): AgentCheckpointData {
        return try {
            val transformedInput = transformLegacyInputFormat(data.lastInput)
            data.copy(lastInput = transformedInput, graphVersion = toVersion)
        } catch (e: Exception) {
            logger.warn(e) { "Input transformation failed, keeping original" }
            data.copy(graphVersion = toVersion)
        }
    }
}

// 3. Configure agent with migration system
val agent = AIAgent(executor, strategy) {
    install(Persistency) {
        storage = PostgresPersistencyStorageProvider(
            persistenceId = "customer-support-v3",
            jdbcUrl = System.getenv("DATABASE_URL")
        )

        // Version management
        strategyId = "customer-support-flow"
        graphVersion = 3
        strategyHasher = DefaultStrategyHasher()
        autoComputeHash = true

        // Chain multiple migrators for complex upgrades
        migrators += NodeRenameMigrator("support", 1, 2)
        migrators += InputFormatMigrator("support", 2, 3)

        // Control checkpoint size
        historyPolicy = MessageCountHistoryPolicy(maxMessages = 50)
    }
}

// 4. Production deployment scenarios
authenticate("bearer") {
    post("/api/agent/resume") {
        val agentId = call.parameters["agentId"]!!

        // Automatic migration during checkpoint restoration
        val checkpoint = agent.persistency().rollbackToLatestCheckpoint(context)

        when {
            checkpoint != null -> {
                call.respond("Resumed from checkpoint ${checkpoint.checkpointId} (migrated to v${checkpoint.graphVersion})")
            }
            else -> {
                call.respond("Starting fresh session")
            }
        }
    }
}

// 5. Runtime execution with automatic migration
agent.run("Process customer inquiry") // ✅ Loads old checkpoint, migrates automatically
agent.run("Handle support ticket")    // ✅ Uses migrated state seamlessly
agent.run("Generate response")        // ✅ All operations work with evolved strategy
```

This unified approach provides safe strategy evolution for production deployments, handling node renaming, input format changes, graph restructuring, and message history optimization.

## Implementation Details

### Core Components

#### Versioned Checkpoints
- `AgentCheckpointData` - Enhanced with version metadata fields
- `CheckpointMigrator` - Interface for version upgrade logic
- Backwards compatible - all new fields optional with defaults

#### Hash Validation System
- `StrategyHasher` - Suspend interface for async hash computation
- `HashComputationResult` - Sealed class for robust error handling
- `DefaultStrategyHasher` - FNV-based deterministic hashing

#### Migration Pipeline
- Sequential migrator application
- Version validation and future-proofing
- Hash mismatch warnings (non-blocking)
- Comprehensive error handling and logging

### Hash Computation with Error Handling

```kotlin
sealed class HashComputationResult {
    data class Success(val hash: String) : HashComputationResult()
    data class Failed(val reason: String, val cause: Throwable? = null) : HashComputationResult()
    data object Unavailable : HashComputationResult()
}

interface StrategyHasher {
    suspend fun computeHash(strategy: AIAgentStrategy<*, *>): HashComputationResult
}

// Error-resilient usage
val config = PersistencyFeatureConfig().apply {
    strategyHasher = DefaultStrategyHasher()
}

when (val result = config.computeAndSetHash(strategy)) {
    is HashComputationResult.Success -> {
        logger.info { "Strategy hash: ${result.hash}" }
    }
    is HashComputationResult.Failed -> {
        logger.warn { "Hash computation failed: ${result.reason}" }
        // Continue without hash validation
    }
    is HashComputationResult.Unavailable -> {
        logger.debug { "Hash computation not configured" }
    }
}
```

